.SH DESCRIPTION
Retrieves the list of all breakpoints currently set in the debugger for
this session.
The function sends a \f[CR]list_breakpoints\f[R] request on
\f[CR]CHAN_DEBUG\f[R] (channel 4) and allocates an array of
\f[CR]bc_breakpoint_t\f[R] structures with the server\(cqs response.
.PP
The caller receives a heap\-allocated array through \f[CR]*bps\f[R] and
the number of elements through \f[CR]*count\f[R].
The caller must free this array by calling
\f[CR]bc_breakpoint_list_free(*bps, *count)\f[R].
.PP
If no breakpoints are set, \f[CR]*bps\f[R] is set to NULL and
\f[CR]*count\f[R] is set to 0.
This is not an error.
