.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
The returned array is a snapshot of breakpoints at query time.
Breakpoints may be added or removed between the query and subsequent
operations.
.IP \(bu 2
The \f[CR]hit_count\f[R] reflects the total number of times the
breakpoint has fired since it was created, including during the current
command if execution is stopped at the breakpoint.
.IP \(bu 2
String fields (\f[CR]kind\f[R], \f[CR]pattern\f[R],
\f[CR]condition\f[R]) are heap\-allocated copies.
Always use \f[CR]bc_breakpoint_list_free()\f[R] to avoid leaks.
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: the client library is not thread\-safe.
